  "notes": "Immature/IMx frontman solo out of the Chris Stokes / TUG camp, 2003–2009. The research names \"two modes — a 93–97 straight kit with 2&4 clap and continuous 16th hats, and a 60–68 half-time bed with clap-on-3, a single kick per bar and no hats\"; the straight mode is the base because seven of the ten sourced tempos sit at 80 or above. Three drum deltas: a clap stacked flat on 2 and 4 with `offGridMs` 0, a continuous 16th hat at 0.62 fill density — high for this section — and a kick with `lockTo808` at 0.5, which is what ties the kit to the sub. This is a true 808 model: \"808 sub on roots with a short slide; sub-forward on the slow jams\" is the whole low end, so `drums.bass808` carries role `bassline` and there is deliberately **no** `bassline` block, because on this schema the two cannot both sound. Harmony is \"two-chord minor vamps with a bell/plucked riff\". \"High tenor with falsetto flips as the ornament, thin doubled harmony, hook of 4–5 pitches\" is the high register with a real octave-jump probability (the falsetto flip), a 4–5 pitch motif and a counter density of 0.32. ⚠ Confidence is **low**: the research rates the entry medium-low and marks the key claim `[LOW-CONF]`, so the keys are lane-level. ⚠ Every velocity, density and portamento number is INFERRED. ⚠ **`chords.harmonicRhythm` re-weighted (2026-08-17, harmony variety floor).** The entry's harmony line is \"two-chord minor vamps with a bell/plucked riff\", and the engine's `vamp` value is *one* chord held for the whole clip (`generators::chords`: \"One chord for the whole pattern\") — so weighting `vamp` at the top rendered a **one**-chord bed the research nowhere describes. The chord motion the entry states is now carried by `1_per_bar` (the pair over a 2-bar cell) and `2_bars_per_chord` (the pair over a 4-bar cell), with `vamp` kept as the minority for the held reading. ⚠ The split between those two rates is **INFERRED** — the entry names the device, not its rate.",
